      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Cardiac pain is a key symptom for diagnosis of myocardial ischemia in man, even if a minority of transient myocardial ischemic episodes are painful. A multiparametric monitoring approach - associating non-invasive and invasive monitoring techniques during transient myocardial ischemia with and without pain - allows to achieve a clinical diagnosis and obtain information about the pathophysiology of the anginal syndrome."},
